# Flutter Conventions

## Widgets — always classes, never methods

```dart
// ❌ BAD — widget as method
Widget _buildHeader() {
  return Container(...);
}

// ✅ GOOD — widget as class
class HeaderWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  const HeaderWidget({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Container(...);
  }
}
```

## Core abstractions

Use app-level abstractions instead of direct package calls:

| Abstraction | Wraps | Location |
|-------------|-------|----------|
| `AppNetwork` | Dio | `core/network/` |
| `AppCache` | SharedPreferences | `core/cache/` |
| `AppEnv` | flutter_dotenv | `core/env/` |

```dart
// ❌ BAD — direct Dio usage in feature
final response = await Dio().get('/api/news');

// ✅ GOOD — through abstraction
final response = await appNetwork.get('/api/news');
```

## Environment variables

Use `flutter_dotenv` via `AppEnv`. Store the base URL and sensitive keys in `.env`:

```
BASE_URL=https://cosmos-back.onrender.com
```

Never hardcode URLs or keys in Dart files.

## Named routes

All navigation uses named routes defined in `core/routes/`:

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Navigator.push(context, MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => NewsPage()));

// ✅ GOOD
Navigator.pushNamed(context, AppRoutes.news);
```

## No unnecessary comments

Do not add comments that just describe what code does. Only comment non-obvious intent or trade-offs.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
// Creates a new instance of NewsBloc
final bloc = NewsBloc(getNewsUseCase);

// ✅ GOOD — no comment needed, the code is self-explanatory
final bloc = NewsBloc(getNewsUseCase);
```
